pokeheartgold-widepointers.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies it to build/pokeheartgold, after pokeheartgold-compile.patch): the
pointer pass's first rule for HeartGold/SoulSilver on a 64-bit host (docs/hgss.md, "Pointer rules"). GENERATED, never
edited by hand: on a working copy with the earlier patches applied, `python3 tools/pokehg_widen.py --tsv`, then
`git -C build/pokeheartgold diff -U2 -- '*.c' '*.h'` (against the earlier patches) below this header.
- port/UINTPTR.tsv's BASE-IN-INT rows whose holder is a parameter or a local (the decomp's Ghidra-typed C keeps an
  address in an s32/u32 and adds DS-layout offsets to it): that parameter, in the definition and in every prototype of
  the function (by position), and that local become intptr_t (s32, int) or uintptr_t (u32, unsigned): 52 files at the pin a53ce07bc
  (95d5f7f1d: 1,111; the HGSS side lifted most holders since). A value stored in
  one is no longer cut to 32 bits; the callers' pointers convert as before.
- Not rules here: the NUM-HOLDS-PTR rows (an address loaded from memory as a number) and "loaded as s32": their offsets
  are a DS layout, lifted into struct fields on the HGSS side first (port/OFFSETS.tsv); "root is s32", "int base" and
  struct fields: no single holder. The pointer casts clang still reports: pokeheartgold-widepointers2.patch.

